      "body": "",
      "button_link": "",
      "button_text": "",
      "description": "OEM and ODM projects often involve more than simply producing a finished product. Designs may need to be reviewed for manufacturability, materials may need to be matched or substituted, and prototypes may require several rounds of adjustment before production.\n\nNESS connects product development with manufacturing through a structured process. We review drawings, dimensions, materials, construction, and finishing requirements before sampling. After the prototype is evaluated and approved, the specifications are transferred into batch production, with quality checks throughout manufacturing and before shipment.\n\nThis approach helps reduce communication gaps between design and production while keeping the approved product specifications consistent from sample to final delivery.",
      "display_name": "",
      "focus_point": "center",
      "gallery": [],
      "images": [],
      "overlay_depth": "0.95",
      "poster_media_key": null,
      "poster_url": "",
      "section_key": "rich_text-1786701276054",
      "section_type": "rich_text",
      "settings": {},
      "sort_order": 4,
      "subtitle": "",
      "title": "How We Solve OEM & ODM Manufacturing Challenges",
      "translations": {},
      "video_media_key": null,
      "video_url": ""
    },
    {
      "body": "",
      "button_link": "",
      "button_text": "",
      "description": "01 — Drawing & Reference Review\nReview drawings, dimensions, reference products, images, and project requirements.\n\n02 — Material & Finish Confirmation\nConfirm fabrics, wood, metal, stone, colors, finishes, hardware, and other specifications.\n\n03 — Prototype & Sampling\nDevelop the first sample or prototype for evaluation and adjustment.\n\n04 — Approval & Production Preparation\nConfirm approved specifications, production details, and quality requirements before batch manufacturing.\n\n05 — Batch Production\nManufacture according to the approved sample, drawings, materials, and specifications.\n\n06 — Quality Control\nInspect dimensions, structure, materials, finishes, assembly, and overall product quality.\n\n07 — Packing & Container Loading\nProducts are packed according to project or customer requirements and prepared for shipment.",
      "display_name": "",
      "focus_point": "center",
